WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.620
So right after Hurricane Andrew came through, it . . . I don't know what it done.

2
00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:11.660
It changed the environmental out there some kind of way.

3
00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:17.120
And them reefs took up . . . I mean, they formed oysters like out of this world.

4
00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:25.340
This boat that I got up there on this wall would leave my house at four o'clock in the morning and run to Lake Pelto.

5
00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:28.180
That's a six-hour run.

6
00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:32.540
And come back with as much as 300 sacks of oysters sitting on the deck of that boat.

7
00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:34.700
When you looked at one, you looked at them all.

8
00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:38.520
They was all pretty round, single oysters, big oysters.

9
00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:41.580
And what caused it, I really don't know.

10
00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:45.080
I think the river was kind of high that year or something.

11
00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:50.880
I don't know exactly what really changed it but something changed it.

12
00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:59.780
An oyster is an animal that's going to tell you the environmental how it is.

13
00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:00.760
Earl?

14
00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:08.140
Yeah, I mean, I think that last statement, Buddy, is kind of the crux of the whole thing.

15
00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:10.620
It's an animal that's on the bottom.

16
00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:13.260
It never moves once it sets on the bottom.

17
00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:16.120
It's only in the water column as a larvae for two to three weeks.

18
00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:21.540
Once it sets to the bottom, it cements to the bottom and will never move again.

19
00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:26.600
And it does become a good environmental sentinel for what's happening in the estuaries.
